{
  "Name": "Okta - Authentication & Sessions - Okta User Sessions Started from Different Geolocations",
  "Description": "Alert: Okta\nGroup: Authentication & Sessions\nMITRE ATT&CK: Initial Access / T1078\nSchedule: every 15 minutes over the previous 15 minutes (edit the scheduled search to change it)\nTuning: okta_user_allowlist / okta_ip_allowlist keys \"<login without domain>|Okta User Sessions Started from Different Geolocations\" or \"<ip>|Okta User Sessions Started from Different Geolocations\"\n\nDetects one user with successful Okta sessions (user.session.start) from more than one country: each successful session in the search window is checked against the user's successful sessions in the 4 hours before it. Two countries within a few hours usually means shared or stolen credentials or a VPN/proxy hop. An inner query finds the users; each alert is one real session per country so the context shows where each came from. Risk floor High (75).\n\nFalse positives: travel with in-flight or airport Wi-Fi, users on corporate VPN exits in another country. Tune with okta_user_allowlist (user|Okta User Sessions Started from Different Geolocations).\n\nLimitations: sessions that straddle two windows are not compared. Okta's own New Country / Velocity behaviors are covered by 'Okta Sign-In with Elevated Risk or New Behavior'.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/initial_access_okta_user_sessions_started_from_different_geolocations/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/tree/main/rules/integrations/okta/initial_access_okta_user_sessions_started_from_different_geolocations.toml",
  "GUID": "0688b6b7-1bf0-5181-93b5-9c28513a405d",
